# A register whose only write in the loop is guarded on a false
# predicate: ptxas stores once, at param_0, 4 B, but the guarded add is
# read as a counter step on every trip, 16 B unique.
RUN: %ptxroof analyze %fixtures/micro/guarded_step.ptx | FileCheck "%s"
CHECK: kernel micro_guarded_step
CHECK: st.global.u32  global store 4 B  warp: 1 sector (ideal 1)  [4 * k[$L__BB0_1] + param_0]  k[$L__BB0_1]: +4 B/iter
CHECK: global bytes per CTA over the loop's own blocks: requested 16 B, unique 16 B, in sectors 128 B
